@startuml consolidation
!include style.iuml
title Memory that cleans itself: consolidation
participant "Writer" as w
participant "Jev" as jev
participant "Code" as code
database "Graph" as g
participant "Claude" as cl

w -> jev : every 20 writes:\nnew note vs its 3 nearest older neighbours\n(order-neutral questions)
jev --> code : same question, different answer? outdated? reports a change?\nstates every fact of the other? repeated episode?
code -> code : order by timestamp\n(tie → latest date in text → who reports the change)
code -> g : older note ➜ **superseded_by** newer
code -> g : fully covered ➜ **duplicate_of / subsumed_by**
code -> g : unorderable ➜ **contradicts** + conflict proposal
code -> cl : repeated episodes ➜ "write the general pattern"
cl -> g : memory_resolve (new semantic note)
note right of g
  Nothing is ever deleted.
  Stale notes stay searchable, rank lower,
  and are skipped by SessionStart.
end note
@enduml
